 kit platform - lists the services, toolchains, tools, and settings kit runs with

   one of
   *kit platform*  lists the services, toolchains, tools, and settings kit runs with

     --text   --json   --jq
                           prints the stages as text, even on a terminal

   --stages      prints the stages, one per line, in order, the same over any workspace
   --marks       prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what the stage
                 draws does: a hash of kit.yml for settings; for toolchains and tools, of the files
                 the toolchains and the dependency providers pin from and of those that keep kit's
                 choice; and for services, of all of those, the clone's git configuration, which
                 holds its remotes, and .kit/policy
   services      each capability kit fills and the service that answers it: hosting, review, ci, and
                 releases, the primary's forge; tracking, each tracker prefix; the project
                 toolchain; each dependency provider whose manifest and lock are here; and the
                 policy engine
   toolchains    each toolchain kit can use, one row for each role it fills, as kit toolchains lists
                 them
   tools         each tool the chosen toolchain and the dependency providers pin, as kit tools lists
                 them
   settings      each key the settings schema names: the value kit.yml sets, or the schema's default


 kit platform
